# Reviewer gate: only reviewed candidates become canonical. A
# logic:FormalizationCandidate in the canonical, axiom-bearing state
# (logic:CandidateAccepted) is legitimate ONLY with a recorded reviewer decision
# (logic:reviewedBy) whose object is an auditable node (IRI or blank node) — not a
# free literal. A plain-literal reviewer value is indistinguishable from a free
# text annotation and cannot be machine-audited; it does not satisfy the governance
# requirement. An accepted candidate with no node-valued reviewer decision — exactly
# the shape of an LLM extraction promoted straight to canonical, or a candidate
# annotated with a bare string rather than a proper reviewer node — is a governance
# violation. Any returned row is a violation (LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed
# formalization governance).
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?candidate WHERE {
    ?candidate a logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
               logic:candidateLifecycle logic:CandidateAccepted .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
        ?candidate logic:reviewedBy ?reviewer .
        FILTER(isIRI(?reviewer) || isBlank(?reviewer))
    }
}
ORDER BY ?candidate
